Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Stop dereferencing possibly-freed pointertype.def in tpointerdef.done (fpc 0.99)
License: expat

compiler/symdef.inc's tpointerdef.done disposes the pointed-to def
only if it is the unresolved forwarddef that this pointerdef
allocated.  The original check is:

    if assigned(pointertype.def) and
       (pointertype.def^.deftype=forwarddef) then
     begin
       dispose(pointertype.def,done);
       pointertype.reset;
     end;

The `pointertype.def^.deftype' read is a use-after-free in the common
case.  Once pdecl.resolve_type_forward replaces the forward by the
real resolved def, `pointertype.def' aliases a def owned elsewhere
(typically by a sibling in the same symtable).  At unit teardown the
symtable destroys its elements in some order; whenever the target
runs destruction before the pointerdef, the subsequent
`pointertype.def^.deftype' read in tpointerdef.done is reading
already-freed memory.

Native FPC tolerated this because the stale bytes almost never held
the ordinal value of `forwarddef' and the read otherwise caused no
observable effect.  Under the tp2cc C++ bootstrap the read is caught
at runtime as a heap-use-after-free in p_tpointerdef::p_done(), with
the freeing site pointing at the sibling t_arraydef destruction
earlier in the same tindexarray::clear() pass.

Fix: track forwarddef ownership with an out-of-band boolean flag on
tpointerdef, set at init time and cleared by pdecl when the forward
gets resolved.  The destructor relies on the flag instead of reading
through a potentially-stale pointer.  PPU-loaded pointerdefs never
own a forwarddef (forwards are a parse-time construct), so they
always set the flag to false.

--- a/compiler/symdefh.inc
+++ b/compiler/symdefh.inc
@@ -158,6 +158,15 @@
        tpointerdef = object(tdef)
           pointertype : ttype;
           is_far : boolean;
+          { True while pointertype.def is an unresolved forwarddef that
+            this pointerdef allocated and therefore owns. Cleared by
+            pdecl.resolve_type_forward once the forward is replaced by
+            the real resolved def (which is owned elsewhere). The
+            destructor relies on this flag instead of reading
+            pointertype.def^.deftype, because at unit teardown the
+            pointed-to real def may already have been freed by a sibling
+            in the same symtable. }
+          has_forward : boolean;
           constructor init(const tt : ttype);
           constructor initfar(const tt : ttype);
           constructor initdef(p : pdef);
--- a/compiler/symdef.inc
+++ b/compiler/symdef.inc
@@ -1421,6 +1421,8 @@
         pointertype:=tt;
         is_far:=false;
         savesize:=target_os.size_of_pointer;
+        has_forward:=assigned(pointertype.def) and
+                     (pointertype.def^.deftype=forwarddef);
       end;


@@ -1431,6 +1433,8 @@
         pointertype:=tt;
         is_far:=true;
         savesize:=target_os.size_of_pointer;
+        has_forward:=assigned(pointertype.def) and
+                     (pointertype.def^.deftype=forwarddef);
       end;


@@ -1460,16 +1464,26 @@
          pointertype.load;
          is_far:=(readbyte<>0);
          savesize:=target_os.size_of_pointer;
+         { PPU-loaded pointerdefs never own a forwarddef -- forwards are a
+           parse-time construct; PPU streams store resolved references. }
+         has_forward:=false;
       end;


     destructor tpointerdef.done;
       begin
-        if assigned(pointertype.def) and
-           (pointertype.def^.deftype=forwarddef) then
+        { Only dispose the pointed-to def if it is the unresolved
+          forwarddef we allocated ourselves.  We must NOT dereference
+          pointertype.def here to find that out: at unit teardown the
+          resolved target may already have been freed by a sibling in
+          the same symtable, and reading .deftype would be a
+          use-after-free.  The has_forward flag carries the ownership
+          fact out-of-band. }
+        if has_forward and assigned(pointertype.def) then
          begin
            dispose(pointertype.def,done);
            pointertype.reset;
+           has_forward:=false;
          end;
         inherited done;
       end;
@@ -1573,6 +1587,7 @@
          pointertype.load;
          is_far:=false;
          savesize:=target_os.size_of_pointer;
+         has_forward:=false;
       end;


--- a/compiler/pdecl.pas
+++ b/compiler/pdecl.pas
@@ -932,6 +932,10 @@
                     tokenpos:=stpos;
                     { we don't need the forwarddef anymore, dispose it }
                     dispose(hpd,done);
+                    { pointerdef no longer owns a forwarddef; destructor
+                      must not try to dispose whatever pointertype.def
+                      now points at. }
+                    ppointerdef(pd)^.has_forward:=false;
                     { was a type sym found ? }
                     if assigned(srsym) and
                        (srsym^.typ=typesym) then
